# Session document rebuild (Nov 2026)

Structural entity changes rebuild the Remote Compose document; variable updates do not.
One Remote Compose document holds every page. Live values are USER vars (no redraw).

## Anti-flash (MAIN front/back swap)

`RemoteDocumentController` keeps a front/back `RemoteComposePlayer` pair.

- Incoming buffer paints at **full alpha behind** the current page (`prepareHiddenDraw(coverCurrentPage=true)`). The first document of a session still uses alpha 0 until PAGE sticks. Stock Android still calls `draw()` at alpha 0; the blank frame was from hiding the old view before Compose raised the new one.
- Restore **scroll and `USER:page` before** the covered draw, then invalidate. Restoring after the covered paint leaves the raised frame at scroll 0.
- Wait a **second covered frame** so long lists finish layout, then flip `mainFrontIsPrimary` and set `replacedMainPlayer`. Do not `GONE` the old buffer in that callback.
- `RemoteDocumentStack` calls `hideReplacedMainPlayer()` from a **SideEffect** after composition records the new zIndex, before the frame draws — not “after placement.”
- `showSlots` / a later `render` must not `GONE` `mainInactive` while `pendingMainSwap` or `replacedMainPlayer` is set.
- `ScreenRenderer.render(..., initialPage = …)` — bake the tablet’s current page into `Vars.PAGE` so a rebuild does not open on home before the player restores page.
- Prefer vars for live values. Timed `refreshEvery` on media (etc.) caused home flashes — only use when the document tree itself must change (forecast lists, to-do rows). Calendar agenda still uses `refreshEvery(60)` + store TTL; a real content change still replaces the document.
- A two-state icon (binary sensor, cover, person) is `toggleIcon` on `USER` on/off. Do not `structural` that glyph: motion, a door, or someone arriving used to rebuild the one document and force-send every picture.
- A sensor reading, an `update` entity, and the weather temperature are variables. Only a baked drawing (the weather condition icon, a forecast list, a history line, the calendar agenda) is `structural` or `refreshEvery`.
- `beginPictureFetch` does not fetch a source key the player already has. A replaced document copies those bitmaps onto the hidden buffer. Camera stills still update when `refreshSeconds` elapses or the source key changes. Video and search stay on the forced (new document) path.
- Music playhead: HA `media_position` is a snapshot plus `media_position_updated_at`. RPI's `NowPlayingTrackTime` adds elapsed time while playing. `mediaPosition()` does that math; `tickProgress` sends only the changed `pos` / `progress` vars — no rebuild. `PlayerHub` applies each debounced snapshot (`conflate` + `collect`, so a slow refresh is not cancelled).

## Energy dashboard across rebuilds

A MAIN rebuild used to clear `energyDashboards`, so the native charts vanished until `SessionMedia.sendEnergyDashboard` arrived (~0.5s blink).

- Protocol: `Document.energyPages: List<Int>? = null`. **Null** = older add-on omitted it → keep existing dashboards. **Empty** = this screen has none. Server sends distinct energy dashboard pages on MAIN documents when rebuilt with that field.
- `RemoteScreenState.withDocument` uses `retainedEnergyDashboards(message)` instead of always dropping.
- `playingEnergyDashboard` prefers the dashboard whose revision matches the current document, else the last one on that page.
- Overlay key is `key(tileId, page)` only — do not key by revision or the composable remounts.
- Overlay bounds for Energy: measure the visible MAIN buffer first, then `documentPlayer`. Keep the last non-null Energy `Rect` while the dashboard is still playing. If bounds are still null, paint the dashboard `fillMaxSize` so the RC hole stays covered.
- `DocumentOverlays` keeps a sticky last Energy dashboard for the current page across a brief `playingEnergyDashboard == null` gap after a MAIN rebuild.
- Compose overlays are composed **after** every Remote Compose `AndroidView` (not interleaved). A MAIN buffer swap otherwise drew the Energy stub over the native dashboard for a frame.
- Capable players get a blank PAGE-coloured Energy hole (`supportsEnergyDashboard`); the update prompt is only for older APKs.
- `withEnergyDashboard` ignores a wrong-rev or identical re-send (same-content refresh still pushes Energy); only a changed payload replaces the message.

## Rebuild and the card overlay

`TapOutcome.Rebuild` rebuilds `Slot.MAIN`. A card is its own document in `Slot.OVERLAY` (`SessionDocument.openCard`), so card-local UI state changed by a tap is not redrawn by that alone. `PlayerSession.rebuildTappedOverlay` also rebuilds the slot the tap came from when it is not MAIN; `show` skips the send when the bytes are unchanged. A card that reads session UI state also needs it from `RenderDataRepository.forCard`, which returns only what each card kind asks for (the vacuum card gets `vacuumUi` and `vacuumRooms`).

## Helpers

- `RenderedDoc.structureChanged` / `isTimedRefreshDue` — split from `stale` for clearer session host logic.
- Thermostat: mode in `structural` when layout depends on `usesDualSetpoint()` so Heat ↔ Heat/Cool rebuilds the dial keys.
- `SessionDocument.show` skips send when `RenderedDoc.hasSameContent` (bytes + navigationDrawer).

## Scroll survives a rebuild

Replacing the document used to start every `verticalScroll` / `horizontalScroll` at the top.

- `keptVerticalScroll` / `keptHorizontalScroll` (`ScrollKeep.kt`) put a stable component id on each scroller. Ids are `0x60_0000` plus a hash of a name (`lights.<tile>.rooms`, `calendar.<tile>`, `freeform.<node>`, …), above video (`0x5C`), map (`0x5D`) and search (`0x5E`).
- The player copies those offsets onto the new document (`DocumentScroll.kt`) **before** the covered swap is shown. The position float is what paint reads; the touch expression would otherwise write 0 back until the next drag. Copy `mMaxScrollY` / `mMaxScrollX` (and the touch expression's max) with the offset.
- When the new bytes match the document already on screen, `SessionDocument.show` keeps that document and only sends changed vars and pictures.

## Nov 24 2026 flash (not released)

Branch `fix/document-flash`, cut from `main` at `0aed4de7` (add-on and player 0.2.69). The work is uncommitted on that branch until someone commits it. The Samsung tablet (SM-T725, serial `R32R5006XNT`, player 0.2.69) still flashes until this add-on is rebuilt and the player reconnects.

The visible flash was a burst of JPEG decodes (`W/HWUI Image decoding logging dropped`, dozens of lines in one or two seconds), not a one-frame jump to home. One document holds every page, so a picture fetch for any page decodes on the player that is showing.

What it was not:

- The urgent "Water shutoff not confirmed" alert. That is `Slot.ALERT` with a scrim. The user saw the flash well before it. A 75-second recording of the Automations page at 30 fps, after the earlier bursts, had no pixel change.
- The Saturday Nov 21 full-screen Assist mic overlay. The mic is a document icon (`sys.assist_mic`) on 0.2.69.
- An alpha Remote Compose bug. Alpha24 is why a baked value must replace the whole document, and why the covered swap exists (the player still draws at alpha 0). The library already updates named variables in place. This flash was the add-on rebuilding that document and then fetching every picture again. The decodes arrived after the swap, on the page already showing.

What caused the bursts on the night of Nov 23–24 (tablet `10.11.0.87`, device `b66d30bc-7d2d-4ef8-b720-0f4609f4ba26`, America/New_York):

- Home Assistant HTTP 502 from 23:47:26–23:48:57 and 23:52:53–23:54:23. Reconnect ("Connected to Home Assistant 2026.11.2") at 23:49:27 and 23:54:53. The next state emit rebuilt the document. Image bursts at 23:49:28, then about every 60 seconds through 23:55:35 (`refreshEvery` is 60 while a calendar or to-do is on any page). Disconnect does not clear `_states`.
- `binary_sensor.front_door_camera_motion` on at 00:09:04. The icon was `structural`, so the document bytes changed and `sendPictures(isForced = true)` ran. HWUI burst 00:09:19–00:09:20, about 15 seconds later, which is the snapshot fetch. A front-door camera HLS 404 at 23:52 only flipped `cam_waiting` / `cam_still` and did not rebuild the document.

Fix on the branch: two-state icons (binary sensor, cover, person) use `toggleIcon`. Weather temperature is a variable; only the condition icon stays structural. `beginPictureFetch` skips a source key already sent. Camera stills still refresh when `refreshSeconds` elapses (default 60). A rebuild can still happen for a forecast, a history line, the calendar agenda, the to-do list, an alarm arm change, or a map when someone moves, and those must not resend pictures the tablet already has.

`DocumentFlash` fails `:server:detekt` if a `structural` lambda reads a live value or if picture send takes `isForced`.

## Check

`DocumentFlash` (detekt, `detekt-rules`) fails the build when a `structural` lambda reads a live value (`temperature`, `humidity`, `numericState`, `updatedLabel`, `lastChanged`, …) or when `beginPictureFetch` / `sendPictures` take `isForced` and would resend a bitmap the player already has. It runs with `:server:detekt` on every change.

Render tests lock the cases detekt cannot see: a motion icon and a sensor or switch reading (`TileIconMotionTest`), a weather temperature (`WeatherNowStructureTest`), and an unchanged picture (`ShownDocumentPictureTest`).

```bash
./gradlew :detekt-rules:test :server:detekt :server:test \
  --tests '*TileIconMotionTest' --tests '*WeatherNowStructureTest' --tests '*ShownDocumentPictureTest'
```
